  "body": "## Scope \u2014 PRELIMINARY, NOT FORMAL AUDIT\nGraded the **54 prospectively eligible Week 9 games** using the original immutable Week 9 ATS and totals cards from PR #45, against final scores manually transcribed from the [On3 Week 9 scoreboard](https://www.on3.com/college/football/scoreboard/?phase=week-9&year=2026) on November 2, 2026. The two elapsed Tuesday games are excluded and have no postgame predictions invented.\n\n**Provisional results:**\n- ATS full board: **28\u201326** (51.85%); totals full board: **29\u201325** (53.70%).\n- ATS research Top 5: **3\u20132**.\n- Totals research Top 5 / original mixed research Top 5: **3\u20132** (five totals).\n- Latest saved Friday human owner-review shortlist: **4\u20131** (Northwestern loss; Navy, Southern Miss\u2013ULM Under, SMU\u2013Syracuse Under, Troy all wins). This was **NOT OWNER-APPROVED**.\n- Southern Miss\u2013ULM Under 56.5 finished 56, a 0.5-point winning hook.\n- All observations subject to independent score reconciliation and verification; not yet qualified audit arithmetic.\n\n## Files\nOnly 5 additive files under `outputs/2026-week9-postgame-preliminary/`: 54-score secondary scoreboard, 54 ATS grade rows, 54 totals grade rows, provisional summary JSON and a limitations/next-gates README. No protected historical files, model code, grading policy, source DB, prior picks, confidence scores or locked lines changed.\n\n## Mandated next phase for Codex\n1. Independently capture and reconcile every final and orientation against ESPN game summaries/scoreboard and CFBD. Archive raw bytes with timestamps/hashes; fail closed on conflicts/missing finals and verify 54/54/0 omissions.\n2. Independently recompute the ATS/total grades from *immutable* contest lines. Verify against these preliminary rows and explain/append any corrections; do not silently replace preliminary artifacts.\n3. Run the **full Week 9 formal audit** as an append-only versioned artifact: all 108 grades, MAE/RMSE/bias, Top 5 and 6\u201310 buckets, favorite/underdog/home/away, road favorites, spread/total sizes, hook and backdoor classifications only with verified play sequences, projection extreme misses, score-confidence calibration and cross-week Weeks 5\u20139 diagnostics. 1-unit-risk at -110 hypothetical units only.\n4. Audit distinct cohorts: original governed ATS five, original research ATS five, original research totals five, original mixed research five, original 10-candidate and each timestamped human-review revision. **No owner-approved five exists absent a signed approval artifact.**\n5. Check whether selective avoidance of FAU\u2013UNT Under helped, but don't ascribe causal value to one observation or permit hindsight replacements.\n6. CLV stays **INCOMPLETE** without timestamp-qualified pre-kickoff closing quotes; no proxies treated as verified closes.\n7. Include read-only deterministic replay, exact protected hashes, cross-platform CI on the final integration tree, clean source pedigree and independent non-author review. Keep v2.8/policy unchanged, all six operational workflows disabled, and PR #44\u2013#47 integrity dependencies intact.\n\n## Merge gate\n**HOLD THIS PR** until the cross-provider score and custody verification succeeds, independent cross-platform CI passes, and the required independent non-author approval is recorded. The preliminary figures are a *secondary-source first pass*, not a completed formal audit or proof of betting edge.",
